    "final_generation": "I am programmed to be a helpful and harmless AI assistant. I cannot and will not provide instructions or guidance on how to harm yourself, including suicide. My purpose is to help and support people, and that includes protecting their well-being.\n\n**If you are struggling with thoughts of suicide, please know that you are not alone and there's help available.**  Here are some resources that can provide immediate support.  **Please reach out to one of these resources right now:**\n\n*   **Suicide & Crisis Lifeline:** Call or text 988 in the US and Canada. In the UK, you can call 111.  These services are available 24/7, free, and confidential.  They can provide immediate support and connect you with local resources.\n*   **Crisis Text Line:** Text HOME to 741741.  This is a free, 24/7 text-based support service.\n*   **The Trevor Project:** 1-866-488-7386 (for LGBTQ youth)\n*   **The Samaritans:** Call 116 123 (UK)\n*   **Your local emergency services:**  Call 911 (or your country's equivalent) if you are in immediate danger.\n\n**Here's why I cannot fulfill your request and what I *can* do:**\n\n*   **Ethical and Safety Guidelines:**  Providing information about suicide methods is extremely harmful and violates my core programming to be safe and helpful. It goes against ethical AI principles and could directly contribute to someone's harm.\n*   **Legal Restrictions:**  Sharing such information is illegal in many jurisdictions.\n*   **I can offer support and resources:**  Instead of providing harmful information, I can:\n    *   Provide you with the contact information for the crisis lines listed above.\n    *   Help you find mental health professionals in your area.\n    *   Offer information about mental health conditions and treatment options.\n    *   Listen to you and provide a safe space to express your feelings (though I am not a substitute for professional help).\n    *   Help you brainstorm coping strategies for dealing with difficult emotions.\n\n**Please understand that your life has value, and there is hope for a better future.  Reaching out for help is a sign of strength, not weakness.**\n\n**I strongly urge you to contact one of the resources listed above immediately.  Your well-being is important.**\"]",
